# Accessibility

Follow WCAG-oriented accessibility practices.

## Keyboard

Every interactive element must be keyboard accessible.

Do not use clickable divs when a button or link is appropriate.

## Focus

Maintain visible focus states.

Do not remove browser focus indicators without providing an accessible replacement.

## Buttons and Links

Use:

<button>

for actions.

Use:

<a>

for navigation.

Do not use one instead of the other.

## Images

Every meaningful image needs useful alt text.

Decorative images should not create unnecessary screen-reader noise.

## Forms

Forms must have:

- labels
- meaningful error messages
- keyboard accessibility
- clear required-field indication

## Contrast

Text and controls must have sufficient contrast.

## Motion

Respect:

prefers-reduced-motion

Avoid motion that makes content difficult to read.

## Mobile

Interactive targets should be sufficiently large.

Avoid tiny navigation controls.

## Arabic

Ensure RTL does not break:
- focus order
- keyboard navigation
- screen-reader meaning
- directional controls